      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is unsafe as written.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** The maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin is generally 2,550 mg/day (about 850 mg three times daily), and lower doses are typical for many patients. A 5,100 mg/day dose carries a high risk of lactic acidosis and gastrointestinal toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe order may have a typo, such as 1700 mg intended as a total daily dose, or 850 mg or 500 mg per dose. It could also be a different formulation or intent.\n\nPlease have the prescribing physician or a licensed clinician confirm the intended dose. Once they do, they can give me the corrected dose, frequency, and route, and I can enter it. Because this is a medication order, it should come from a clinician who is responsible for the patient's care."
      }
